<title>GHANA: Ghana issues new coins to replace worn notes.</title>
<headline>Ghana issues new coins to replace worn notes.</headline>
<dateline>ACCRA 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ghana's Central Bank issued new 200 and 500 cedi coins on Tuesday to replace notes which are rapidly wearing out.</p>
<p>Central Bank secretary Alex Bernasko told Reuters that the coins would circulate alongside the notes until all the notes were withdrawn.</p>
<p>The bank declined comment on speculation that it plans to issue a 10,000-cedi note.</p>
<p>($1=1,740 cedis)</p>
</text>
